<title>UK: Prism orders 44 trains from Adtranz.</title>
<headline>Prism orders 44 trains from Adtranz.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>British railway operator Prism Rail Plc said on Tuesday it has placed an order worth for around 220 million stg for the delivery of 44 new four-car trains from Germany's Adtranz.  </p>
<p>It said in a statement that Adtranz, the rail joint venture between Germany's Daimler-Benz, and Swiss-Swedish engineering group ABB, would manufacture and maintain the trains and that it would lease the trains from Porterbrook Leasing Company Ltd.</p>
<p>The trains are due to be delivered and in service by November 1999.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
